<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38409" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπᾰφ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαφάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>touch, touching, handling,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				46b
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφυγμοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Marcellin.
					<u>Puls.</u>
					114
				</span></i>
			, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. μωσικὰ [τῆς
			λύρας</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Euryph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.39.27
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαφαὶ χειρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.2d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>severe handling, punishment,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. καὶ νουθεσία</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				46d
			</span></i>; esp. of Pythagorean <i>treatment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>VP</u>
				15.64
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				25.114
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>touch, contact,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδεῖα ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IGRom.</u>
					4.503.11
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			metaph., of <i>apprehension,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				250
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τοῦ ἀγαθοῦ εῐτε γνῶσις εἴτε ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					6.7.36
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Comm.Math.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ μέλλοντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Myst.</u>
					3.26
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> Geom.,
				<i>point of contact,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				<u>Phaen.</u>
				p.68
			</span></i> M., <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Hyp.</u>
				2.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ἐπαφῶν,</span> on the
			theory of <i>tangents,</i> title of work by Apollonius of Perga,
				<i><span class="en">
				Papp.
				636.21
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the sense of touch,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				186b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in phrases
			such as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτὸς ἱερᾶς νόσου καὶ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLips.</u>
					4.20
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλὴν ἐ. καὶ ἱ. ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					94.11
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>, etc., prob. <i>external claim,</i> cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>PStrassb.</u>
				79.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
